## 4. Exclusion List

Do not include:

- Model selection, vendor comparisons, or the LLM landscape — Marcus didn't mention it and this audience doesn't need a vendor guide
- AI safety, AI ethics, or responsible AI frameworks — not the article's lane; would dilute the ROI argument
- Small or mid-market AI adoption — every signal in this transcript points to enterprise C-suite; 101 content would undermine credibility
- Technical implementation detail — how models work, what infrastructure is required, MLOps practices
- Historical AI hype cycles (AI winters, 2016 hype, etc.) — Marcus didn't reference it; adds historical context nobody asked for
- Adjacent topics like generative AI vs. predictive AI distinctions — not relevant to the ROI framework argument
- Generic "AI is transforming every industry" framing — exactly the kind of talking point this article exists to replace

